Slurm opens the paths in `#SBATCH --output/--error` BEFORE the job script runs, so a `mkdir -p`
inside sbatch_pet_fullevent_nominal.sh cannot save it: if this directory is missing, the job holds
its queue slot for however long the wait is and then dies instantly at dispatch with nothing to read.

This file exists so the directory exists in every checkout. Same fix, same reason, as
nd-unfolding/pet/powered_closure/logs/.gitkeep -- that launcher's header records the identical
lesson. Do not delete it because it "looks empty".

Found 2026-08-06 while pre-flighting RESTORE Step 4: the directory was absent on the cluster tree and
the job would have wasted the queue wait.
